  "content": {
    "raw": "<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"la-authority-page\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group la-authority-page\">\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This page summarises selected scientific publications, lymphatic surgery training and media features related to lymphedema diagnosis, prevention and surgery. It is intended as an educational reference for patients, therapists and referring clinicians.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p><em>Information on this site is for education only and is not a substitute for personalised medical advice.</em></p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2>Lymphatic surgery training</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column {\"width\":\"58%\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-column\" style=\"flex-basis:58%\">\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Dr Jeremy Sun completed an MOH Health Manpower Development Plan (HMDP) fellowship in Tokyo focused on comprehensive lymphedema management across all severities, training under Professor Takumi Yamamoto and Professor Akitatsu Hayashi.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The training focus included holistic multi-disciplinary lymphedema care, lymphatic imaging, conservative therapy pathways and lymphatic surgery, including supermicrosurgical lymphovenous anastomosis (LVA) and treatment planning for more advanced disease.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This background informs LymphedAsia’s approach: lymphedema is not treated as a single-operation problem, but as a staged condition requiring diagnosis, imaging, pressure-flow assessment, surgical selection, compression therapy and long-term follow-up.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column {\"width\":\"42%\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-column\" style=\"flex-basis:42%\">\n<!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/hmdp-certificate-lymphedema-surgery-training.jpg\" alt=\"HMDP certificate for holistic multidisciplinary lymphedema management and lymphatic surgery training\"/><figcaption>SingHealth Health Manpower Development Plan Award 2022 for holistic multi-disciplinary lymphedema management and lymphatic surgery.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image -->\n</div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"akitatsu-training-photos\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group akitatsu-training-photos\">\n<!-- akitatsu-hayashi-training-photos -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Japan lymphatic surgery training</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:columns -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":4817,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dr-jeremy-sun-akitatsu-hayashi-lva-training-microscope.jpg\" alt=\"Dr Jeremy Sun with Professor Akitatsu Hayashi during microscope-based LVA and lymphatic surgery training in Tokyo\" class=\"wp-image-4817\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Microscope-based LVA and lymphatic surgery training in Tokyo with Professor Akitatsu Hayashi.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n<!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":4818,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dr-jeremy-sun-akitatsu-hayashi-ramses-2025.jpg\" alt=\"Dr Jeremy Sun with Professor Akitatsu Hayashi at RAMSES 2025 robotic assisted microsurgery symposium in Japan\" class=\"wp-image-4818\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Continuing international microsurgery exchange at RAMSES 2025 in Japan.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns -->\n</div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2>Peer-reviewed lymphatic surgery publications</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list --><ul>\n<li><strong>Lymphovenous shunts in the treatment of lymphedema.</strong> <em>Journal of the Chinese Medical Association.</em> 2024;87(1):5–11. DOI: 10.1097/JCMA.0000000000001016. <a href=\"https://journals.lww.com/jcma/fulltext/2024/01000/lymphovenous_shunts_in_the_treatment_of_lymphedema.3.aspx\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Read the article</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Primary surgical prevention of lymphedema.</strong> <em>Journal of the Chinese Medical Association.</em> 2024;87(6):567–571. DOI: 10.1097/JCMA.0000000000001101. <a href=\"https://journals.lww.com/jcma/fulltext/2024/06000/primary_surgical_prevention_of_lymphedema.1.aspx\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Read the article</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Genital elephantiasis: surgical treatment and reconstruction.</strong> <em>Journal of the Chinese Medical Association.</em> 2024;87(2):142–147. DOI: 10.1097/JCMA.0000000000001021. <a href=\"https://journals.lww.com/jcma/fulltext/2024/02000/genital_elephantiasis__surgical_treatment_and.2.aspx\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Read the article</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>The 1+X technique: A novel microsurgical approach for secondary lymphedema.</strong> <em>Journal of Plastic, Reconstructive &amp; Aesthetic Surgery.</em> 2025. <a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1748681525005881\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">View article page</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Current Insights into Post-Traumatic Lymphedema.</strong> <em>Trauma Care.</em> 2025;5(4):24. <a href=\"https://www.mdpi.com/2673-866X/5/4/24\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Read the article</a>.</li>\n</ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2>Prevention and health-system research</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>In addition to peer-reviewed publications, Dr Sun has contributed to research on the health-economic evaluation of lymphedema prevention strategies. A Research Square preprint examines <strong>immediate lymphatic reconstruction versus structured surveillance</strong> for preventing breast cancer-related lymphedema after axillary surgery. As a preprint, it should be interpreted as work under review rather than a final peer-reviewed guideline.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p><a href=\"https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-8722507/v1\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Cost-Effectiveness of Immediate Lymphatic Reconstruction Versus Structured Surveillance for Preventing Breast Cancer–Related Lymphedema After Axillary Surgery</a>. Research Square preprint. DOI: 10.21203/rs.3.rs-8722507/v1.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2>How this research informs patient care</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list --><ul>\n<li><strong>Patient selection:</strong> not every patient with lymphedema is best treated by the same operation.</li>\n<li><strong>Imaging and mapping:</strong> ultrasound and ICG lymphography can help identify remaining lymphatic channels and guide bypass planning.</li>\n<li><strong>LVA quality:</strong> in lymphovenous bypass surgery, leakage, pressure gradients and venous reflux can influence how well a bypass functions.</li>\n<li><strong>Prevention:</strong> lymphedema prevention after cancer surgery requires weighing immediate reconstruction, structured surveillance, patient risk and local healthcare pathways.</li>\n<li><strong>Advanced disease:</strong> severe lymphedema may require staged reconstructive planning rather than a single procedure.</li>\n</ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2>Related patient education pages</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list --><ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://lymphedasia.com/dr-jeremy-sun-lymphedema-specialist/\">Dr Jeremy Sun — lymphedema specialist in Singapore</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://lymphedasia.com/lva-surgery-singapore/\">LVA surgery in Singapore</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://lymphedasia.com/lymphedema-surgery-singapore/\">Lymphedema surgery options in Singapore</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://lymphedasia.com/why-lva-quality-matters-lymphovenous-bypass/\">Why LVA quality matters: leakage, pressure and venous reflux</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://lymphedasia.com/genital-lymphedema-causes-symptoms-treatment/\">Genital lymphedema: symptoms, assessment and treatment options</a></li>\n</ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2>Media appearances</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Selected media and conference features related to lymphedema screening, diagnosis, lymphatic imaging and reconstructive surgery.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\">\n<!-- wp:image --><figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/cna-lymphedema-interview-screenshot.jpg\" alt=\"Channel NewsAsia media feature thumbnail about early screening and relief for lymphoedema patients\"/><figcaption>Channel NewsAsia: early screening and relief for lymphoedema patients.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>Channel NewsAsia (CNA)</strong><br/>Early screening able to provide relief for lymphoedema patients.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\">\n<!-- wp:image --><figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/8world-lymphedema-service.jpg\" alt=\"8world media feature thumbnail about Changi General Hospital lymphedema treatment service\"/><figcaption>8world: CGH lymphedema treatment service and screening technology.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>8world</strong><br/>樟宜综合医院设立淋巴水肿治疗服务处，引进新筛查技术。</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->\n<!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\">\n<!-- wp:image --><figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/cgh-caring-lymphedema-diagnosis-treatment.jpg\" alt=\"Changi General Hospital Caring feature thumbnail about lymphedema diagnosis and treatment\"/><figcaption>CGH Caring: lymphedema diagnosis and treatment.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>Changi General Hospital — Caring</strong><br/>A leg-up in lymphoedema diagnosis and treatment.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\">\n<!-- wp:image --><figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/medical-channel-asia-icg-lymphography.jpg\" alt=\"Medical Channel Asia feature thumbnail about ICG fluorescence imaging for lymphoedema\"/><figcaption>Medical Channel Asia: ICG fluorescence imaging for early lymphoedema detection.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>Medical Channel Asia</strong><br/><a href=\"https://medicalchannelasia.com/medical-investigations/seeing-the-invisible-icg-fluorescence-imaging-detects-lymphoedema-early/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Seeing the Invisible: ICG Fluorescence Imaging Detects Lymphoedema Early</a>.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->\n<!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\">\n<!-- wp:image --><figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/singhealth-speaker-jeremy-sun.jpg\" alt=\"Dr Jeremy Sun speaker thumbnail for SingHealth Duke-NUS conference breast cancer surgery programme\"/><figcaption>SingHealth Duke-NUS Conference programme listing.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>SingHealth Duke-NUS Conference</strong><br/>Programme listing related to breast cancer surgery.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\">\n<!-- wp:image --><figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/nhk-lymphedema-documentary.jpg\" alt=\"NHK lymphedema documentary thumbnail featuring lymphedema education\"/><figcaption>NHK documentary-related lymphedema media thumbnail.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>NHK</strong><br/>Lymphedema documentary-related educational media.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->\n</div><!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>Related:</strong> <a href=\"/ultrasound-mapping-lva-surgery-singapore/\">Ultrasound mapping for LVA surgery</a> explains why high-frequency ultrasound can identify lymphatic targets even when ICG linear patterns are absent in selected patients.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>Core guide:</strong> <a href=\"/lymphedema-treatment/\">Lymphedema treatment in Singapore</a> explains how diagnosis, compression therapy, ICG lymphography, ultrasound mapping, LVA and advanced-stage surgery fit into a complete treatment pathway.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
    "rendered": "\n<div class=\"wp-block-group la-authority-page is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<p>This page summarises selected scientific publications, lymphatic surgery training and media features related to lymphedema diagnosis, prevention and surgery. It is intended as an educational reference for patients, therapists and referring clinicians.</p>\n<p><em>Information on this site is for education only and is not a substitute for personalised medical advice.</em></p>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Lymphatic surgery training</h2>\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-28f84493 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\"><div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:58%\">\n<p>Dr Jeremy Sun completed an MOH Health Manpower Development Plan (HMDP) fellowship in Tokyo focused on comprehensive lymphedema management across all severities, training under Professor Takumi Yamamoto and Professor Akitatsu Hayashi.</p>\n<p>The training focus included holistic multi-disciplinary lymphedema care, lymphatic imaging, conservative therapy pathways and lymphatic surgery, including supermicrosurgical lymphovenous anastomosis (LVA) and treatment planning for more advanced disease.</p>\n<p>This background informs LymphedAsia’s approach: lymphedema is not treated as a single-operation problem, but as a staged condition requiring diagnosis, imaging, pressure-flow assessment, surgical selection, compression therapy and long-term follow-up.</p>\n</div><div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:42%\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/hmdp-certificate-lymphedema-surgery-training.jpg\" alt=\"HMDP certificate for holistic multidisciplinary lymphedema management and lymphatic surgery training\" title=\"\"><figcaption>SingHealth Health Manpower Development Plan Award 2022 for holistic multi-disciplinary lymphedema management and lymphatic surgery.</figcaption></figure>\n</div></div>\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group akitatsu-training-photos is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<!-- akitatsu-hayashi-training-photos -->\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Japan lymphatic surgery training</h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-28f84493 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dr-jeremy-sun-akitatsu-hayashi-lva-training-microscope.jpg\" alt=\"Dr Jeremy Sun with Professor Akitatsu Hayashi during microscope-based LVA and lymphatic surgery training in Tokyo\" class=\"wp-image-4817\" title=\"\" srcset=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dr-jeremy-sun-akitatsu-hayashi-lva-training-microscope.jpg 1280w, https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dr-jeremy-sun-akitatsu-hayashi-lva-training-microscope-300x225.jpg 300w, https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dr-jeremy-sun-akitatsu-hayashi-lva-training-microscope-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dr-jeremy-sun-akitatsu-hayashi-lva-training-microscope-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Microscope-based LVA and lymphatic surgery training in Tokyo with Professor Akitatsu Hayashi.</figcaption></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dr-jeremy-sun-akitatsu-hayashi-ramses-2025.jpg\" alt=\"Dr Jeremy Sun with Professor Akitatsu Hayashi at RAMSES 2025 robotic assisted microsurgery symposium in Japan\" class=\"wp-image-4818\" title=\"\" srcset=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dr-jeremy-sun-akitatsu-hayashi-ramses-2025.jpg 1280w, https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dr-jeremy-sun-akitatsu-hayashi-ramses-2025-300x225.jpg 300w, https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dr-jeremy-sun-akitatsu-hayashi-ramses-2025-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dr-jeremy-sun-akitatsu-hayashi-ramses-2025-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Continuing international microsurgery exchange at RAMSES 2025 in Japan.</figcaption></figure>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Peer-reviewed lymphatic surgery publications</h2>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Lymphovenous shunts in the treatment of lymphedema.</strong> <em>Journal of the Chinese Medical Association.</em> 2024;87(1):5–11. DOI: 10.1097/JCMA.0000000000001016. <a href=\"https://journals.lww.com/jcma/fulltext/2024/01000/lymphovenous_shunts_in_the_treatment_of_lymphedema.3.aspx\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Read the article</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Primary surgical prevention of lymphedema.</strong> <em>Journal of the Chinese Medical Association.</em> 2024;87(6):567–571. DOI: 10.1097/JCMA.0000000000001101. <a href=\"https://journals.lww.com/jcma/fulltext/2024/06000/primary_surgical_prevention_of_lymphedema.1.aspx\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Read the article</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Genital elephantiasis: surgical treatment and reconstruction.</strong> <em>Journal of the Chinese Medical Association.</em> 2024;87(2):142–147. DOI: 10.1097/JCMA.0000000000001021. <a href=\"https://journals.lww.com/jcma/fulltext/2024/02000/genital_elephantiasis__surgical_treatment_and.2.aspx\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Read the article</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>The 1+X technique: A novel microsurgical approach for secondary lymphedema.</strong> <em>Journal of Plastic, Reconstructive &amp; Aesthetic Surgery.</em> 2025. <a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1748681525005881\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">View article page</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Current Insights into Post-Traumatic Lymphedema.</strong> <em>Trauma Care.</em> 2025;5(4):24. <a href=\"https://www.mdpi.com/2673-866X/5/4/24\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Read the article</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Prevention and health-system research</h2>\n<p>In addition to peer-reviewed publications, Dr Sun has contributed to research on the health-economic evaluation of lymphedema prevention strategies. A Research Square preprint examines <strong>immediate lymphatic reconstruction versus structured surveillance</strong> for preventing breast cancer-related lymphedema after axillary surgery. As a preprint, it should be interpreted as work under review rather than a final peer-reviewed guideline.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-8722507/v1\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Cost-Effectiveness of Immediate Lymphatic Reconstruction Versus Structured Surveillance for Preventing Breast Cancer–Related Lymphedema After Axillary Surgery</a>. Research Square preprint. DOI: 10.21203/rs.3.rs-8722507/v1.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How this research informs patient care</h2>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Patient selection:</strong> not every patient with lymphedema is best treated by the same operation.</li>\n<li><strong>Imaging and mapping:</strong> ultrasound and ICG lymphography can help identify remaining lymphatic channels and guide bypass planning.</li>\n<li><strong>LVA quality:</strong> in lymphovenous bypass surgery, leakage, pressure gradients and venous reflux can influence how well a bypass functions.</li>\n<li><strong>Prevention:</strong> lymphedema prevention after cancer surgery requires weighing immediate reconstruction, structured surveillance, patient risk and local healthcare pathways.</li>\n<li><strong>Advanced disease:</strong> severe lymphedema may require staged reconstructive planning rather than a single procedure.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Related patient education pages</h2>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://lymphedasia.com/dr-jeremy-sun-lymphedema-specialist/\">Dr Jeremy Sun — lymphedema specialist in Singapore</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://lymphedasia.com/lva-surgery-singapore/\">LVA surgery in Singapore</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://lymphedasia.com/lymphedema-surgery-singapore/\">Lymphedema surgery options in Singapore</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://lymphedasia.com/why-lva-quality-matters-lymphovenous-bypass/\">Why LVA quality matters: leakage, pressure and venous reflux</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://lymphedasia.com/genital-lymphedema-causes-symptoms-treatment/\">Genital lymphedema: symptoms, assessment and treatment options</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Media appearances</h2>\n<p>Selected media and conference features related to lymphedema screening, diagnosis, lymphatic imaging and reconstructive surgery.</p>\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-28f84493 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\"><div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/cna-lymphedema-interview-screenshot.jpg\" alt=\"Channel NewsAsia media feature thumbnail about early screening and relief for lymphoedema patients\" title=\"\"><figcaption>Channel NewsAsia: early screening and relief for lymphoedema patients.</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Channel NewsAsia (CNA)</strong><br/>Early screening able to provide relief for lymphoedema patients.</p>\n</div><div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/8world-lymphedema-service.jpg\" alt=\"8world media feature thumbnail about Changi General Hospital lymphedema treatment service\" title=\"\"><figcaption>8world: CGH lymphedema treatment service and screening technology.</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>8world</strong><br/>樟宜综合医院设立淋巴水肿治疗服务处，引进新筛查技术。</p>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-28f84493 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\"><div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/cgh-caring-lymphedema-diagnosis-treatment.jpg\" alt=\"Changi General Hospital Caring feature thumbnail about lymphedema diagnosis and treatment\" title=\"\"><figcaption>CGH Caring: lymphedema diagnosis and treatment.</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Changi General Hospital — Caring</strong><br/>A leg-up in lymphoedema diagnosis and treatment.</p>\n</div><div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/medical-channel-asia-icg-lymphography.jpg\" alt=\"Medical Channel Asia feature thumbnail about ICG fluorescence imaging for lymphoedema\" title=\"\"><figcaption>Medical Channel Asia: ICG fluorescence imaging for early lymphoedema detection.</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Medical Channel Asia</strong><br/><a href=\"https://medicalchannelasia.com/medical-investigations/seeing-the-invisible-icg-fluorescence-imaging-detects-lymphoedema-early/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Seeing the Invisible: ICG Fluorescence Imaging Detects Lymphoedema Early</a>.</p>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-28f84493 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\"><div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/singhealth-speaker-jeremy-sun.jpg\" alt=\"Dr Jeremy Sun speaker thumbnail for SingHealth Duke-NUS conference breast cancer surgery programme\" title=\"\"><figcaption>SingHealth Duke-NUS Conference programme listing.</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>SingHealth Duke-NUS Conference</strong><br/>Programme listing related to breast cancer surgery.</p>\n</div><div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://lymphedasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/nhk-lymphedema-documentary.jpg\" alt=\"NHK lymphedema documentary thumbnail featuring lymphedema education\" title=\"\"><figcaption>NHK documentary-related lymphedema media thumbnail.</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>NHK</strong><br/>Lymphedema documentary-related educational media.</p>\n</div></div>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong>Related:</strong> <a href=\"/ultrasound-mapping-lva-surgery-singapore/\">Ultrasound mapping for LVA surgery</a> explains why high-frequency ultrasound can identify lymphatic targets even when ICG linear patterns are absent in selected patients.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Core guide:</strong> <a href=\"/lymphedema-treatment/\">Lymphedema treatment in Singapore</a> explains how diagnosis, compression therapy, ICG lymphography, ultrasound mapping, LVA and advanced-stage surgery fit into a complete treatment pathway.</p>",
